     "page": 1,
     "text": "Scott and Cardenas Clinic\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI am writing to provide a detailed summary of the recent consultation with Ms. Jennifer Saunders, which took place on November 9, 2025. She presented with vitamin D deficiency, among other chronic conditions.\n\nMs. Saunders has a history of an eating disorder, which she has successfully managed for approximately 9.8 years. Currently, her condition is well-controlled, and she does not require any medications for this issue. \n\nAdditionally, Ms. Saunders was diagnosed with diffuse large B-cell lymphoma about 10 years ago, which is now in a controlled state following her treatment. She is not on any medications for this condition at the moment.\n\nVitamin D deficiency, which was the primary reason for her recent visit, is also well-managed. She is taking ergocalciferol 50000 IU as prescribed.\n\nHer hypothyroidism, which started in November is currently well-controlled with levothyroxine 100 mcg daily. \n\nSeasonal allergies, noted since May 2022, are being managed with fluticasone nasal spray 50 mcg and loratadine 10 mg as needed.\n\nFurthermore, her urinary tract infection from May 2019 is under control. She is taking sulfamethoxazole-trimethoprim 800/160 mg and nitrofurantoin 100 mg as prescribed.\n\nMs. Saunders has been non-compliant with her medication regimen and has missed two follow-up appointments, which is concerning.\n\nSocially, she used to smoke 10 cigarettes per day until she quit in July 2024 and consumes approximately one alcoholic drink per week\n"
