     "text": "Medical Group\nRe: Jennifer Saunders (DOB 05/02/1983)\n\nJune 30, 2025: \nDr. Courtney Hill, attending physician at Henry-Torres Medical Group, saw Jennifer Saunders today for a follow-up regarding a rash. During the visit, her blood pressure was recorded at 118/69 mmHg and her weight at 172 pounds. She appears to be doing well overall, and there were no alarming findings the physical exam. Her diffuse large B-cell lymphoma remains under control, with no new concerning symptoms or signs of relapse noted.\n\nOctober 31, 2024: \nDr. Courtney Hill evaluated Jennifer Saunders on this date for her ongoing management of diffuse large B-cell lymphoma. Her blood pressure was 120/74 mmHg and her weight was 170 pounds. The patient continues to do well, with no evidence of active lymphoma on recent imaging and blood tests. She has been in remission for about 10 years since completing her initial treatment. No new medications were started.\n\nMarch 03, 2024: \nJennifer Saunders was seen by Dr. Courtney Hill on March 3, 2024 for continued follow-up of her diffuse large B-cell lymphoma. At that time, her blood pressure was 116/65 mmHg and her weight 160 pounds. The patient remains in a controlled phase, with no signs of disease progression on recent PET/CT scan. She is doing well with no new complaints or symptoms. Her vital signs were stable and she had no issues.\n\nJuly 05, 2023: \nDr. Courtney Hill attended to Jennifer Saunders on July 5, 2023 for ongoing monitoring of her diffuse large B-cell lymphoma. Her blood pressure was 118/66 mmHg and her weight 167 pounds. The patient is doing well, with no evidence of disease relapse on her recent labs and imaging. She reports no new symptoms and her physical exam was unremarkable aside from a benign rash.\n\nNovember 05, 2022: \nJennifer Saunders was seen by Dr. Courtney Hill on November 5, 2022 for routine follow-up of her diffuse large B-cell lymphoma. Her blood pressure was 117/75 mmHg and her weight 165 pounds. The patient continues to do well, with no signs of active lymphoma on her most recent blood work and imaging. She reports feeling fine with no new complaints. Her exam otherwise unremarkable.\n\nMarch 07, 2022: \nDr. Courtney Hill evaluated Jennifer Saunders on March 7, 2022 for ongoing management of her diffuse large B-cell lymphoma. Her blood pressure was 122/77 mmHg and her weight 172 pounds. The patient remains in remission, with no evidence of disease recurrence on her recent PET/CT scan and blood tests. She is doing well overall with no new issues.\n\nJuly 08, 2021: \nJennifer Saunders was seen b"
